        "original_id": "a8c0045f-727a-5e22-ae58-c99d99c83901",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michaël Llodra, Juan Martín del Potro, Novak Djokovic, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, John Isner, Gaël Monfils\n- Events: 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles\n- Organizations: Association of Tennis Professionals\n- Concepts: tennis rankings, singles and doubles achievements\n\nFacts:\n- Juan Martín del Potro was born on 23 September 1988.\n- Juan Martín del Potro is an Argentinian professional tennis player also known as Delpo.\n- Michaël Llodra won the singles title before the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament and entered that event as the defending champion.\n- At the 2009 ABN AMRO World Tennis Tournament – Singles, Gaël Monfils defeated Michaël Llodra in the second round.\n- Michaël Llodra was a successful doubles player with three Grand Slam championships and an Olympic silver medal.\n- Michaël Llodra also had singles success, winning five career titles.\n- Michaël Llodra earned singles victories over Novak Djokovic, Juan Martín del Potro, Tomáš Berdych, Robin Söderling, Jo-Wilfried Tsonga, Nikolay Davydenko, Janko Tipsarević, and John Isner.\n- Juan Martín del Potro was ranked world No. 24 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals at the time described.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
